Friday Update
* Trade Alert: Sold half of Bit Digital calls for 38% gain* Stocks slide as=
 investors resume worrying about vaccination pace and market volatilityStoc=
ks around the world sank into a broad retreat that extended across industri=
es amid lingering concerns that a surge of retail trading was creating havo=
c and as traders mulled an uncertain outlook for deploying coronavirus vacc=
ines.The S&amp;P 500 Index fell about 2%, turning negative for the year and=
 heading to its biggest weekly decline in three months, Bloomberg reported,=
 as day traders=E2=80=99 bids for heavily shorted stocks fueled speculation=
 hedge funds would need to reduce their market exposure. Small-cap stocks o=
utperformed as Johnson &amp; Johnson said its one-shot vaccine generated st=
rong protection against Covid-19, though it was less effective against the =
South Africa variant.GameStop (GME) and AMC Entertainment (AMC) soared, sig=
naling a return of volatility for stocks popular in internet chat rooms as =
brokerages said they would start to ease trading restrictions imposed after=
 wild swings this week. Bitcoin surged as much as 16% after Tesla Inc. foun=
der Elon Musk mentioned it on his Twitter profile.Global stocks are set for=
 their worst weekly slide in about three months, partly on the turmoil caus=
ed by hoards of day traders hatching stock bets that roiled hedge funds and=
 strained trading platforms. Some strategists say investors should buy the =
dip because they expect stimulus-fueled economic recovery from the pandemic=
. Others fear an uneven vaccine rollout signals a fragile outlook amid stre=
tched valuations.Through 2:45 pm ET, the Dow was down 550 points, or 1.8%, =
while the S&amp;P 500 was off 1.95%, the Nasdaq 100 was down 2% and the Rus=
sell was off 1.8%.Portfolio: We sold first half of BTBT calls at the open o=
n a gap up for 38.5% gain, which is great. Adjust target and stop. No new r=
ecommendations going into the weekend. *NEW RECOMMENDATIONBit Digital Inc. =
(BTBT) February $17.50 calls-- Symbol: BTBT210219C00017500-- Bought at $5.7=
0 on Thursday, Jan 28. -- Sold half at $7.90 at the open for a gain of 38.5=
%!-- Now trading at $4.75-- Sell second half at new $8 lmt gtc-- Set stop a=
t new $4.50 stp *Jon D. MarkmanAll recommendations are for monthly options =
expiring on the third Friday of the specified month unless otherwise noted.=
 All stops are good after 10:30 a.m. Eastern only unless otherwise specifie=
d. All orders are good for the day only unless otherwise noted. "Day only" =
orders expire at the close of the current session. Past results are no guar=
antee of future returns. All accounts may not achieve comparable results. R=
ecommendations are leveraged and speculative, so only use risk capital =E2=
=80=94 i.e., money you can afford to lose. All results are shown ex-commiss=
ions and fees. Options trading involves the risk of substantial loss. Some =
news and research provided by Wall Street Journal, Bloomberg, Associated Pr=
ess, MT Newswires and Reuters.&nbsp;

